.TH SSH\-KEY\-AUDIT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ssh-key-audit \- review a local OpenSSH authorized_keys file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssh-key-audit\fR [\fB--file\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB--help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a local authorized_keys file (default: $HOME/.ssh/authorized_keys). Reports malformed or unrecognized key lines, duplicate blobs, DSA keys, and writable file or directory modes. Never modifies the file. This is a best-effort text audit, not a complete SSH parser or server policy analysis.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-file PATH\fR
Read an explicit authorized_keys file.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Display usage information on standard output.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the command name and version on standard output.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
\fBssh\-key\-audit \-\-file ~/.ssh/authorized_keys\fR
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 no warnings; 1 warnings; other nonzero values indicate an error.
.SH NOTES
This tool is an original SASD implementation inspired by administrative topics in Nate Campi and Kirk Bauer, Automating Linux and Unix System Administration (Second Edition, 2009). No book source code is included.
